<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <!--
      §7.5 Hardened Runtime entitlements.

      DevType is NOT sandboxed and cannot be: a CGEventTap that observes and
      swallows keystrokes system wide is fundamentally incompatible with the App
      Sandbox. The distribution path is therefore Developer ID plus notarization,
      not the Mac App Store.

      Notarization requires the Hardened Runtime (codesign option "runtime").
      Under Hardened Runtime, Apple Events access is needed because
      SettingsDeepLinker opens System Settings panes and the relaunch flow talks
      to other processes.

      Input Monitoring and Accessibility are TCC services, not entitlements. They
      are granted by the user at runtime and must NOT be declared here. Do not add
      com.apple.security.device.* keys; those are sandbox only and will cause
      notarization or launch to fail.

      Deliberately absent:
        com.apple.security.app-sandbox (incompatible, see above)
        com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory
        com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation
      Add the latter two only if a future dependency genuinely requires them. Each
      one materially weakens the runtime and invites notarization scrutiny.
    -->
    <key>com.apple.security.automation.apple-events</key>
    <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
